,1,0,0,0,1],"status":"paired entrance arch module, provisional local registration"},{"id":"part-1629","part":"3022.dat","color":19,"position":[-200,-136,220],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"status":"paired entrance arch module, provisional local registration"},{"id":"part-1630","part":"3022.dat","color":19,"position":[200,-136,220],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"status":"paired entrance arch module, provisional local registration"},{"id":"part-1631","part":"3040b.dat","color":19,"position":[-200,-144,220],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"status":"triangular arch shoulder slope candidate"},{"id":"part-1632","part":"3665a.dat","color":19,"position":[-200,-144,220],"matrix":[-1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,-1],"status":"mirrored inverted shoulder slope candidate"},{"id":"part-1635","part":"3024.dat","color":19,"position":[-220,-152,220],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"status":"paired entrance arch module, provisional local registration"},{"id":"part-1636","part":"3024.dat","color":19,"position":[-180,-152,220],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"status":"paired entrance arch module, provisional local registration"},{"id":"part-1637","part":"92593.dat","color":19,"position":[-200,-160,220],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"status":"paired entrance arch module, provisional local registration"},{"id":"part-1638","part":"11477.dat","color":19,"position":[-200,-168,220],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"status":"paired entrance arch module, provisional local registration"},{"id":"part-1639","part":"3024.dat","color":19,"position":[180,-152,220],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"status":"paired entrance arch module, provisional local registration"},{"id":"part-1640","part":"3024.dat","color":19,"position":[220,-152,220],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"status":"paired entrance arch module, provisional local registration"},{"id":"part-1641","part":"92593.dat","color":19,"position":[200,-160,220],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"status":"paired entrance arch module, provisional local registration"},{"id":"part-1642","part":"11477.dat","color":19,"position":[200,-168,220],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"status":"paired entrance arch module, provisional local registration"},{"id":"part-1643","part":"3460.dat","color":19,"position":[-240,-176,220],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"status":"tan 1x8 tie beam candidate along portal wing"},{"id":"part-1644","part":"3460.dat","color":19,"position":[240,-176,220],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"status":"tan 1x8 tie beam candidate along portal wing"},{"id":"part-1645","part":"4733.dat","color":19,"position":[-240,-184,180],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"status":"tan four-side-stud pier candidate along the paired portal wing"},{"id":"part-1646","part":"4733.dat","color":19,"position":[-240,-184,220],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"status":"tan four-side-stud pier candidate along the paired portal wing"},{"id":"part-1647","part":"4733.dat","color":19,"position":[240,-184,180],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"status":"tan four-side-stud pier candidate along the paired portal wing"},{"id":"part-1648","part":"4733.dat","color":19,"position":[240,-184,220],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"status":"tan four-side-stud pier candidate along the paired portal wing"}],"manual_observations":[{"pages":"16-17","steps":[13,14],"evidence":"Page 16 adds 2 short flat tiles, 7 long flat tiles, 2 small corner elements along three sides of the base perimeter. Page 17 begins a large grey floor panel with one olive 1x? marker tile and paired dark connector pieces; 12 floor tiles/plates are depicted.","placement":"The 12 LDraw 69729 tiles remain a 3x4 field. Their x extent [-80,40] LDU now meets the step18 4x6 mosaic right edge at x=-80; the later step44 choir semicircle is centered at x=0,z=420 beside this floor field. Contact of the arch with the tile field and exact z boundary remain provisional."},{"pages":"18-19","steps":[15,16],"evidence":"Step 15 adds two small tan plates, two tan longer plates, six dark 1x? plates and multiple grey plates to start paired interior footprints. Step 16 continues the floor with repeated dark/tan groups and a long grey edge strip; the 4x,3x,3x,2x and 4x,7x,1x quantities are shown.","placement":"The 24 paired 42862/48165 cells remain a 4x6 mosaic with bounds x=[-320,-80], z=[240,600] LDU. The step14 tile field begins at x=-80, providing an exact nominal edge match; later step44 places the choir arc center at x=0,z=420, 200 LDU east of the mosaic center. Internal color pattern and physical clutch remain provisional."},{"pages":"20-23","steps":[17,18,19,20],"evidence":"Step 17 shows four dark rectangular plates, one tan plate and four round tan studs. Step 18 adds 24 dark and 24 white triangular floor pieces. Step 19 adds 20 round tan studs. Step 20 adds repeated white/black wedge pieces in counts 5,5,8 and 5,5,10.","placement":"Later pages confirm a large repeated triangular nave floor and the axial/twin-bay alignment. They provide a backward constraint for steps 14-16, while leaving the current MPD origin and scale uncertain."},{"pages":"23","steps":[20],"evidence":"Instruction page 23 shows border detail groups with white counts 5/5/8 and black counts 5/5/10. The pieces differ in footprint across three silhouettes and surround the black/white triangular floor patch.","placement":"The 5-count silhouettes map to five complementary 42862/48165 pairs per color; the broad silhouettes map to 8 white 43710 and 10 black 43711 double wedges. The large wedges form two mirrored, concentric semicircular runs centered at x=0,z=420 (r=200 and 250 LDU); shifting the prior center +200 LDU places the choir arc beside the mosaic rather than through its center. The later step44 view shows 13 repeated three-stud top modules along the same choir arc: 13×60/π ≈248 LDU supports the outer radius 250. Exact endpoints, step14 floor contact, and clutch remain provisional."},{"pages":"37","steps":[44],"evidence":"Step 44 adds 13 repetitions each of a tan curved-top brick candidate and a tan 1x3 tile candidate along the outer choir arc. The assembled view shows an approximately semicircular repeated cap over the choir wall; 13 three-stud modules imply radius about 248 LDU.","placement":"Used as a backward geometric constraint for step20: it supports an outer radius near 250 LDU, while exact cap part identification, vertical level, wall connection coordinates, and physical clutch are not yet modeled/verified."},{"pages":"24","steps":[21],"evidence":"Step21 calls for one tan 2x3 plate, one tan 1x2 plate and two tall reinforced 1x2x3 panels. The exploded view puts the 2x3 plate over the first panel, adds the second panel in the next one-stud row, then places the 1x2 plate on the third exposed two-stud row.","placement":"The two 87544 panels are 20 LDU apart along the choir-arc tangent, at successive z rows 400 and 420, with the panel bottom edges at y=-16 and top studs at y=-88. A 3021 plate at y=-96 is rotated to span radial width2 × tangent length3 and covers rows z=400/420/440; 3023b at y=-104 is stacked on the exposed z=440 row. The global arc anchor and physical clutch remain provisional."},{"pages":"25","steps":[22],"evidence":"Step22 shows three repetitions each of a tan 2x3 plate, a tan 1x2 grooved plate with a center stud, and a reddish-brown round 2x2 plate with a center stud. The later choir views show three support pads spaced around the inside of the curved wall. LDraw candidates 3021, 15573 and 18674 match the respective dimensions/silhouettes and callout counts.","placement":"Three stacks are placed symmetrically on an inner choir radius of 200 LDU at angles -60°, 0°, +60° around center (0,420). Each stack has 3021 at y=-16, 15573 at y=-24 and 18674 at y=-32; all are oriented tangent to the arc. The symmetry and inner radius are diagram-derived and remain provisional; connector clutch and exact stud offsets are not physically checked."},{"pages":"26","steps":[23,24,25,26],"evidence":"Steps23-24 each add a tan one-centre-stud 1x2 jumper and one 1x4 articulated hinge silhouette. Step25 adds one tan 2x3 plate. Step26 adds a tan jumper and one reddish-brown 1x2 rounded-end open-stud plate. The official LDraw 35480 silhouette matches the callout.","placement":"Steps23-24 hinge pairs begin a curved upper choir course. The tan jumper silhouette/count is mapped to 15573. Step25 3021 and step26 35480 form an intermediate support pad at theta120 on R200. Step25 3021 and step26 35480 are placed at the 120-degree intermediate R200 support pad; their shared footprint and exact clutch remain provisional."},{"pages":"27","steps":[27,28,29,30],"evidence":"Step27 adds two articulated hinge pairs, one 15573 jumper, one 3021 support cap and one reddish-brown 35480 rounded-end open-stud plate. Step28 adds two more hinge pairs and one jumper; step29 adds five jumpers. Step30 shows the curved module attached over the choir support row. The articulated callout matches the official LDraw 2429/2430 hinge-plate pair.","placement":"Six 2429/2430 pairs form a provisional curved course on a 230-LDU centerline, with hinge joints at 40,60,80,100,120,140 degrees. At 80 LDU per 1x4 module, their 20-degree chord pitch matches this radius and the run ends near the step22 support angles 30 and 150 degrees. The 40-LDU radial plate width spans radii 210-250, reaching both the R200 support plates and R250 step20 outer arc. Ten 15573 pieces are placed as the sequence jumpers/crown row and two 3021 plates cap the intermediate R200 supports at theta60 and theta120. Exact layer heights, curved-piece overlap, and physical clutch remain provisional; the two 35480 pieces sit atop the theta60/120 support caps; their exact orientation and clutch remain provisional."},{"pages":"28-29","steps":[31,32,33,34,35,36],"evidence":"Step31 adds a single articulated hinge module and jumper; step32 adds a tan plain 1x2 plate. Step33 adds two hinge modules with a 2x3 cap, tan jumpers, a brown 35480 rounded-end plate and a plain 1x2 cap. Step34 adds three hinge modules with the same support/plate family. Step35 adds six tan centre-stud jumpers along the upper choir curve; step36 adds one white 1x1 round plate at the terminal end.","placement":"Steps31-34 form a second provisional articulated course directly above the first at R230, reusing its six hinge axes. The three tan 15573 connectors attach at the course start, middle and end; six step35 jumpers cap the row. The step32 plate extends the endpoint support, and steps33/34 support stacks are placed at intermediate R200 pads theta60 and theta120 using the exploded layer sequence. Step36 white 4073 sits at the R250 terminal point theta180. Exact local attachment offsets and physical clutch remain provisional."},{"pages":"31-33","steps":[38,39,40],"evidence":"Step38 adds two tan 1x1 bricks, two tan 1x2 plates, one reinforced 1x2x3 panel and one smooth grey 1x1 round tile. Step39 adds six each of 1x1 bricks, 87544 panels and grey round tiles; its inset places a tile and brick on the panel top studs. Step40 adds fourteen white 1x2 plates, twenty-eight white 1x1 plates, fourteen black 1x1 side-stud bricks and fourteen black 2x1 curved-top bricks. LDraw candidates 3005, 3023b, 3024, 5907, 87087, 87544 and 98138 match the illustrated silhouettes and quantities.","placement":"Step38 panel is drafted at theta180 and the six step39 radial piers at theta15,45,75,105,135,165 on R230; their panels rise from y=-16 to -88 and their top tile/brick occupy opposite studs. Two tan risers sit at the two R200 endpoints. Step40 builds fourteen repeated details at half-circle angles (i+0.5)×180/14 on R250: white 1x2 base, two white 1x1 plates, one black side-stud brick and one black curved-top brick. Part counts are diagram-confirmed; exact angular registration and curved-part contact are provisional."}]}
